{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: reordered the hyperparameter priors so that `sigma_alpha`, `sigma_beta`, and `sigma_gamma` are sampled before they are used as prior scales for `alpha`, `beta`, and `log_gamma`. Replaced the indexed likelihood statements `y[n] ~ bernoulli_logit(...)` inside the loop with a deterministic computation of `eta` followed by the equivalent vectorized protected observation `y ~ bernoulli_logit(eta)`. The data file is unchanged; `J`, `K`, `N`, `jj`, and `kk` are context inputs, not protected observations.
","model_safe_stan":"/**
 * HIERARCHICAL PL2
 */

data {
  int<lower=1> J; // number of students
  int<lower=1> K; // number of questions
  int<lower=1> N; // number of observations
  array[N] int<lower=1, upper=J> jj; // student for observation n
  array[N] int<lower=1, upper=K> kk; // question for observation n
  array[N] int<lower=0, upper=1> y; // correctness of observation n
}
parameters {
  real delta; // mean student ability
  array[J] real alpha; // ability for student j - mean ability
  array[K] real beta; // difficulty for question k
  array[K] real log_gamma; // discriminativeness for question k
  real<lower=0> sigma_alpha; // sd of student abilities  
  real<lower=0> sigma_beta; // sd of question difficulties 
  real<lower=0> sigma_gamma; // sd of log question discriminativeness
}
model {
  vector[N] eta;

  delta ~ cauchy(0, 5);
  sigma_alpha ~ cauchy(0, 5);
  sigma_beta ~ cauchy(0, 5);
  sigma_gamma ~ cauchy(0, 5);
  alpha ~ normal(0, sigma_alpha);
  beta ~ normal(0, sigma_beta);
  log_gamma ~ normal(0, sigma_gamma);

  for (n in 1 : N) {
    eta[n] = exp(log_gamma[kk[n]])
             * (alpha[jj[n]] - beta[kk[n]] + delta);
  }
  y ~ bernoulli_logit(eta);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"J":4,"K":1,"N":5,"jj":[3,1,4,3,1],"kk":[1,1,1,1,1],"y":[1,1,0,0,1]}","protected_variables":["y"]}
